  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Solar Job Creation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Africa is faced with an increasing demand for electricity but limited supply due to an array of challenges with the existing coal powered infrastructure. Solar power is a promising alternative to the current coal fired power generation. Growth of the solar industry is however limited by the availability of skilled labour. Through this project Amandla Development creates a training centre that targets trainees from the population of disadvantaged youth from the Philippi Area in Cape Town. These youth will be supported with soft skills through Amandla&#x2019;s my Journey training program that increase employability. After that, they may participate in a practical solar maintenance training. Part of these trainees will further receive installation training and are expected to enter a promising career in South Africa&#x2019;s growing solar sector.</narrative>
  </description>
